ns, the committee felt that these boats would be too difficult to handle.  Each nation could enter two boats per event.  The " [:a {:href "/results/157608"} "inrigger coxed fours"] " was contested at Stockholm for the only time in Olympic history."] "\n\n" [:p {} "There were no bronze medals awarded in rowing at the 1912 Olympic Games.  The rowing course allowed only two boats at a time, so the finals consisted of only two crews, who won the gold and silver medals.  The losing semi-finalists were not awarded bronze medals, although we have listed the number of semi-finalists by nation below in the medal statistics.  In both the inrigger coxed fours and the coxed " [:a {:href "/results/157617"} "eights"] ", there was only one losing semi-finalist."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157569"} "Single Sculls, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "17 – 19 July 1912"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n" [:td {} "11"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157590"} "Coxed Fours, Outriggers, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "17 – 19 July 1912"] "\n" [:td {} "55"] "\n" [:td {} "9"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157608"} "Coxed Fours, Inriggers, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "17 – 18 July 1912"] "\n" [:td {} "30"] "\n" [:td {} "4"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157617"} "Eights, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "17 – 19 July 1912"] "\n" [:td {} "99"] "\n" [:td {} "8"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n184 (184/0)\n"] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n14 (14/0)\n"] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n\n" [:h2 {} "Medals"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:t